{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And this is the law of the meal-offering.</b> One law for all of them — to require oil and frankincense as stated in the passage. For one might say: Do I know that they require oil and frankincense only for the meal-offering of an Israelite, which is gleaned — the meal-offering of priests, which is entirely consumed, from where? Scripture states: ״תּוֹרַת״ (Sifra)." "<b>He shall bring it near.</b> That is the presenting at the southwestern corner (there)." "<b>Before YHWH.</b> That is the west, which is toward the side of the Tent of Meeting." "<b>Toward the front of the altar.</b> That is the south, which is the front of the altar, for the ramp is placed on that side (Sotah 14)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:12.440791225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}